title: Drop unused POSIX <unistd.h> for embedded portability
updated: 2026-09-29T03:45:22Z
---

The real consumer is bare-metal/RTOS Chan FatFs where <unistd.h> (POSIX) may not
exist. It is included but unused (leftover from the POSIX original, which used lseek/SEEK_SET):
  cdb_seek.c:10, cdb_make.c:10, cdb_make_put.c:11
The SEEK_SET fallback in cdb_seek.c:14-16 is also dead (f_lseek takes an absolute offset).

Confirm nothing in each file references unistd.h/SEEK_SET symbols before removing, then
sh t/compile-check.sh must stay clean. Small, surgical. Lane: tinycdbff-worker.

